      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg/day. The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (labeled max 2,000 mg/day for extended-release). This order is double that. A dose this high raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nSome possible intended orders:\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for IR.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- **500 mg PO two or three times daily**, or another standard titration step. Metformin is usually started low (500 mg once or twice daily) and increased gradually.\n\nPlease check the intended dose and frequency, ideally with your resident or attending. Once you confirm, I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily as written, please tell me the clinical reason and get it confirmed by your supervising physician. I'd still want that confirmation before entering it."
      }
     ],
