       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the problem. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum metformin dose, and I don't see a clinical reason or attending sign-off that would justify it. If it were given, the patient could be harmed.\n\nHere are some ways to move forward:\n- **Enter a dose within the usual range.** For example, 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose if the patient is new to metformin. Tell me which one and I'll enter it.\n- **Check with your resident or attending.** If you think 1,700 mg three times daily was a typo, such as 1,700 mg/day total, they can confirm the intended dose.\n- **Have the attending place the order.** If they truly want a dose above the maximum, they can enter it themselves with the rationale documented. Pharmacy will probably want to review it too.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
